      {
        "narration": "A flower bulb once cost more than a house. Amsterdam, sixteen thirty-seven, and the flower was a tulip.",
        "visual_query": "dutch tulip field colour",
        "visual_fallback": "tulip flowers"
      },
      {
        "narration": "The prized bulbs were streaked with flame patterns. Nobody knew why, and nobody could reliably breed them.",
        "visual_query": "striped tulip petals closeup",
        "visual_fallback": "flower closeup"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Buyers traded contracts in taverns for bulbs still in the ground, months from flowering. Nobody was holding a tulip.",
        "visual_query": "dutch golden age tavern painting",
        "visual_fallback": "old painting"
      },
      {
        "narration": "In February the buyers simply stopped turning up at an auction in Haarlem. Prices fell to nothing within weeks.",
        "visual_query": "haarlem historic dutch street",
        "visual_fallback": "old town street"
      },
      {
        "narration": "The cause was mundane: a virus made the streaks, and the crash hit a small circle of traders. The Dutch economy barely noticed.",
        "visual_query": "tulip bulbs soil planting",
        "visual_fallback": "garden soil"
      }
    ],
